- `-c /tmp` (no statix.toml in /tmp) → hmm, no error, the default config ✓. Hmm, BUT: when I created /tmp/statix.toml (invalid) and ran `-c /tmp/pr` → the error appeared ✓! So the walk-up from /tmp/pr DID find /tmp/statix.toml ✓.
- And without /tmp/statix.toml, `-c /tmp/pr` → no error ✓.
- And `-c /tmp` → hmm, /tmp/statix.toml doesn't exist now → no error ✓.

Hmm, so the walk-up goes all the way to `/` and if nothing is found → the default config, no error ✓.
And `-c /nonexistent` → hmm, an IO error ✓. Hmm, so the path existence check happens first ✓.

Hmm, so: 
```
fn resolve(p):
   if p.is_file(): Ok(Some(p))
   else if !p.exists(): Err(io)
   else: walk up from p; if found → Ok(Some(f)); else → Ok(None)
```
Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and the walk-up starts at p itself ✓ (so `-c /tmp/pr` checks /tmp/pr/statix.toml then /tmp/statix.toml then /statix.toml) ✓.

Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and `-c ""` → hmm, "" doesn't exist → hmm, an IO error ✓ (observed "No such file or directory (os error 2)") ✓.

Hmm, OK. Let me implement:
```
pub fn resolve_config(p) -> Result<Option<PathBuf>, VErr> {
   if p.is_file() { return Ok(Some(p.into())) }
   if !p.exists() { return Err(VErr::Io("No such file or directory (os error 2)".into())) }
   let mut cur = p.to_path_buf();
   loop {
      let cand = cur.join("statix.toml");
      if cand.is_file() { return Ok(Some(cand)) }
      match cur.parent() {
         Some(par) if !par.as_os_str().is_empty() => cur = par.into(),
         _ => return Ok(None),
      }
   }
}
```
Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and for `.` the parent is "" → stop → Ok(None) ✓.

Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and `-c /tmp/pr/q.nix` (a file that exists but isn't valid TOML) → the parse error ✓. Hmm, and `p.is_file()` is true ✓.

Hmm, and what if the target is a file that doesn't exist? Hmm, `p.is_file()` false and `p.exists()` false → an IO error ✓.

Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and what about a file that exists but can't be read (permissions)? Hmm, an IO error ✓.

Hmm, OK. Let me also handle: the config is loaded lazily? Hmm, hmm — hmm, from the observations, `check -c /nonexistent target` → the config error ✓ (so the config is resolved first) ✓.

Hmm, hmm. Hmm, and if the config file doesn't exist (Ok(None)) → the default config ✓.

Let me patch vfs.rs and main.rs.

Then re-test.

